{
 "about": "Tileable CC0 PBR environment textures. tileMeters: real-world size one texture repeat covers. Each material: <name>_color (sRGB), _normal, _rough, _ao (linear) as 2048 px WebP, and _1k variants (1024 px). Built by tools/blender/make-textures.py.",
 "normalConvention": "Normal maps are OpenGL (+Y green up), like glTF and Poly Haven nor_gl. Babylon's glTF loader sets invertNormalMapX = !scene.useRightHandedSystem and invertNormalMapY = scene.useRightHandedSystem for glTF's OpenGL maps; code-built StandardMaterial/PBRMaterial in the game's left-handed scene need the same flags (invertNormalMapX = true, invertNormalMapY = false). Needs one visual check in the game (light from a known side on cobblestone).",
 "roughness": "single-channel greyscale WebP (read the R channel); ao likewise. ao exists only when the source provided one.",
